@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] regional-piece-geometry-parity
Spatial subdivision MUST preserve every source face exactly once, including winding, positions,
per-corner normals, every consumed UV/colour channel and material-slot identity. A declared piece budget
MUST bound every emitted piece under the actual triangle accounting. The partition frame, cell policy
and budget MUST enter the producer's real inputs; unsupported attributes or geometry MUST refuse rather
than disappear. Pieces MUST retain authored pivots and placements, with no cracks or moved seams.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] regional-piece-parent-semantics
Subdivision MUST preserve the logical parent's instance/material grouping, culling policy and shadow
policy. Omitting an unused material slot from a child MUST NOT merge formerly distinct parent groups.
A whole authored collision hull MUST have one declared component owner; render-only children MUST
remain in visual clearance/footprint reads even when another child owns collision. Collision/query
consumers MUST follow their actual ownership and MUST NOT duplicate a whole hull once per visual child.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] final-query-surface-survives-render-partition
Partitioning rendered ground MUST NOT change which final surface owns placement, route or collision
queries. Consumers of a canonical whole surface MUST be explicitly migrated to a complete published
final-surface product before its native parent retires. They MUST NOT silently read natural terrain,
stale parent files or an arbitrary piece. This source contract does not replace native seam/traversal
validation when component/collision boundaries change.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] independent-model-products-are-required-inputs
Where models are separate named products, normal assembly MUST consume the complete current library
and reject missing, stale or altered members. It MUST NOT regenerate a missing model inline or require
an optimization opt-in. Model keys MUST cover their actual geometry, UV/atlas/export helpers, settings
and tools; placements and unrelated material colours MUST NOT become model inputs without a real read.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] regional-membership-retirement-order
Only an explicitly exclusive generated owner MAY retire superseded source members. Every current
model/hull MUST be complete before retirement, and links, escapes, special files or incomplete membership
MUST refuse before deletion. Committed sources and another owner's outputs MUST remain untouched.
Native retirement additionally requires successful current validation/saves and complete existence and
external-reference preflight; a deletion failure MUST prevent a successful import report.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] bounded-pier-runtime-and-riding-ownership
The pier's generated runtime roster MUST replace an oversized parent with its complete bounded children.
It MUST NOT load both the whole parent and those children for rendering or collision. Whole logical riding
queries, rails, placement transforms, collision flags and source face ownership MUST remain preserved.
Every native blocking child MUST use its own current LOD0 collision, without a stale whole-parent override.
The native owner MUST validate every current child and all package sidecars before retiring old members.
Source checks do not replace guarded native collision, seam, traversal and packaged-root acceptance.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;performance] independently-cached-atomic-world-exports
Region geometry MUST be generated and exported as explicit small logical products. Each final
mesh export task MUST own exactly one primary FBX or GLB with at most 32768 triangles, its complete
metadata and declared source/data/tool inputs. Unrelated logical assets MUST NOT share an export
cache key or a region-wide generation callback. One local logical asset edit MUST leave unrelated
geometry/export tasks current when their actual consumed inputs are unchanged. Whole-region source
fingerprints and order-only edges MUST NOT hide or manufacture consumed-data dependencies.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] assemble-small-world-products
Region assembly MUST combine the exact independently owned export inventory, placements and material
bindings without joining the bounded products back into an oversized mesh. Missing, stale, duplicate,
foreign or incomplete products MUST fail before publishing the region manifest. Renames and removals
MUST retire only that owner's superseded generated files after a complete preflight. Every original
face/corner, normal, UV channel/value, colour, material binding, transform and collision contract MUST
be preserved across the logical split; a spatial child MUST NOT reinterpret logical placement keys.
Pieces MUST remain independently imported native mesh assets. A required performance merge,
packed representation or HLOD MUST be an explicit downstream native product after individual
receiving, with its own consumed-piece identities; it MUST NOT force unchanged source pieces
through a whole-parent export or raw reimport.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;performance] mesh-export-dependency-direction
A mesh export MUST consume its own geometry definition, parameters and shared construction primitives.
Exports SHOULD remain independent of sibling mesh exports. Required terrain, boundary, placement and
query prerequisites MUST be explicit validated data products rather than incidental reads of another
exported FBX/GLB whenever the geometry data can be published directly. Assembly consumes the cached
mesh products and performs their logical composition, placement and connections. A shared assembly
manifest MUST NOT become an input to otherwise independent mesh exports.
